# [List available flags]($heading.id('help'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `-h`, `--help` | Off | Print the supported usage. |

# [Model flags]($heading.id('model-and-listener'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--model=<path>` | Required | Path to the model repository. See [Model storage]($link.page('llmd/howto/model-storage')) for directories and supported URIs. |
| `--model-name=<string>` | Derived from model path | Model name reported in the OpenAI API. |
| `--speculative-drafter-model=<path>` | `null` (disabled) | Drafter repository path, or `native` for a built-in drafter. |


# [Bind the listener]($heading.id('bind-the-listener'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--listen=<addr>` | `0.0.0.0:8000` | Address to listen on. |

# [Batching and context]($heading.id('batching-and-context'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--batch-size=<number>` | `16` | Maximum concurrent requests per data shard. |
| `--token-batch-size=<number>` | `1024` | Maximum tokens per data shard in one inference step. |
| `--max-context-len=<number>` | `128000` | Maximum context length in tokens for the model. |
| `--prefill-chunk-size=<number>` | `256` | Maximum tokens processed for a given sequence during chunked prefill. |
| `--speculative-draft-count=<num>` | Derived from model configuration | Number of draft tokens to verify. |
| `--data-parallel=<number>` | `1` | Number of data shards |

# [Memory and cache]($heading.id('memory-and-cache'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--page-chunk-size=<number>` | `16` | Tokens per KV-cache page chunk. |
| `--gpu-memory-fraction=<fraction>` | `0.9` | Fraction of GPU memory available to LLMD. |
| `--cache-memory-fraction=<fraction>` | `0.95` | Fraction of the memory allocated to LLMD by `--gpu-memory-fraction` filled with cache pages after loading the model. |

The memory of the device is divided in 4 parts.
- Driver memory
- Model weights
- User Kv Cache
- Dynamic overhead

When LLMD starts, it allocates up front `--gpu-memory-fraction` on the device. A bit should be left over for the driver.
After the model weights are loaded, LLMD use `--cache-memory-fraction` on the remaining memory to allocate the KV cache, leaving a little bit of memory for runtime allocations.

Normally lack of memory is detected before serving start,
but if a runtime crash is triggered by an OOM, decreasing `--cache-memory-fraction` can help.

```=html
