# [Sampling]($heading.id('sampling'))

These values are sampling fallbacks, rather than launch defaults.

| LLMD option | Fallback | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--top-k=<number>` | `50` | Top-k sampling cutoff. |
| `--top-p=<fraction>` | `1.0` | Nucleus sampling probability threshold. |
| `--min-p=<fraction>` | `0.0` | Minimum nucleus sampling probability threshold. |
| `--temperature=<number>` | `1.0` | Sampling temperature controlling randomness. |

# [System One]($heading.id('systemone'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--systemone-window=<number>` | Batch size / 4 | Number of questions from one `/v1/systemone` request in flight at once. |

# [Misc]($heading.id('misc'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--io-impl=<name>` | `zio` | Zig allows to dynamically change the I/O runtime.
We recommend [zio](https://github.com/lalinsky/zio), but `--io-impl=threaded` is also available using `std.Io.Threaded` |
